      <h2 id="specifying-oc-ocp-jenkins-image_important-changes-to-openshift-jenkins-images" class="group scroll-mt-20">Specifying a fixed <code>oc</code> client version for OpenShift Jenkins images<a href="#specifying-oc-ocp-jenkins-image_important-changes-to-openshift-jenkins-images" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can ensure that your Jenkins pipeline uses your specified <code>oc</code> client version with the Jenkins container image by configuring the version you require.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul><li>Define the <code>oc</code> tool version explicitly in the pipeline configuration to use a specific OpenShift client version in a Jenkins pipeline as shown in the following example:</li></ul>
      <CodeBlock code={"pipeline {\n    agent any\n\n    tools {\n        oc 'oc-4.22'\n    }\n\n    stages {\n        stage('Version') {\n            steps {\n                sh 'oc version'\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}"} lang="terminal" title="Example pipeline configuration:" />
